/-!
# Coherence Theory of Reciprocity Families

Umbrella for the phases between the amplitudes of a family of rows and the columns of a
reciprocity kernel: the wall of the two-estimate frame as a phase `L`-function and the price of
completion; the average row of the cubic-theta probe, which carries no reciprocal of the target;
Poisson summation in the rows (short columns are incoherent, over `ℤ^d` and over `ℤ[ω]`); the Gram
entry of two rows as a completed sum and the diagonal short Gram; the Möbius sign and the angular
twist in the root numbers of the rows. See `CoherenceTheoryOfReciprocityFamilies/README.md`.
-/
